##Day 4 Complete Notes:

**1. Code Cleanliness

-Never write the same selector twice
-Keep the universal reset (*) only once at the top
-Clean code is easier to read and maintain

**2. Flexbox Properties Used

-display: flex → Makes the container a flexbox
-flex-wrap: wrap → Allows items to move to the next line if needed
-gap: 12px → Adds equal spacing between flex items (better than using margin)

**3. Creating Card Style

'''
background: #f0f0f0;
padding: 10px 16px;
border-radius: 6px;
'''

-background → Gives the card a background color
-padding → Adds space inside the card
-border-radius → Makes the corners rounded

**4. Smooth Hover Effect:
'''
transition: 0.3s;
transform: translateY(-3px);
'''

-transition: 0.3s → Makes the change smooth (0.3 seconds)
-transform: translateY(-3px) → Moves the element 3px upward on hover

**5. Why We Use These
-Flexbox + gap → Clean horizontal layout for skills & projects
-Cards → Makes the section look modern
-Transition + Transform → Adds professional hover interaction

**6. Final Responsive Rule

-Always write desktop styles first
-Then add @media queries for mobile
-Always test both desktop and mobile view

##Summary Formula (Day 1 to Day 4):

-HTML = Structure
-CSS = Design
-Flexbox = Alignment
-Gap = Spacing between items
-Border-radius = Rounded corners
-Transition = Smooth effect
-Transform = Movement effect
-Media Query = Mobile responsive
